426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 208 0 R
/E (The work is organised as a design-first study. The first stage defines the problem, the entities, and the constraints. The second stage specifies the state, action, reward, and risk formulations. The third stage describes the simulator, the learning agent, the baselines, and the explanation procedure. The final stage defines how the methods will be compared, what statistical treatment is appropriate, and which limitations must be reported. This ordering allows each design decision to be reviewed before expensive training runs are started.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 208 0 R
/E (Throughout the report, statements about expected behaviour are written as expectations or hypotheses. No measured improvement is claimed, because the framework is presented at the design stage and the controlled experiments described in Chapter 5 remain to be carried out.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
