447 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 209 0 R
/E (Reinforcement learning models an agent that observes a state, chooses an action, receives a reward, and transitions to a new state. Sutton and Barto provide the standard theoretical treatment [16]. Deep Q-networks learn control policies from experience [3], while Proximal Policy Optimisation is a policy-gradient approach designed for stable updates [4]. These are candidate methods for the assignment agent. Nazari et al. studied reinforcement learning for vehicle-routing problems [5], and Kool et al. investigated attention-based route construction [6]. Xu et al. explored learning and planning for large-scale ride-hailing dispatch [7], while Lin et al.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
448 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 209 0 R
/E (studied multi-agent reinforcement learning for fleet management [8]. These works support the )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
