/T (Reproducibility requires storing random seeds, configuration, model version, and evaluation settings. Reliability requires explicit handling of infeasible assignments and missing features. Interpretability requires explanations to reflect the actual decision factors. Scalability requires practical state construction and candidate scoring as the fleet grows. Maintainability requires clear interfaces between simulator, policy, baseline, risk, explanation, and reporting modules. Data integrity requires a clear distinction between simulated and real observations.)
/E (Reproducibility requires storing random seeds, configuration, model version, and evaluation settings. Reliability requires explicit handling of infeasible assignments and missing features. Interpretability requires explanations to reflect the actual decision factors. Scalability requires practical state construction and candidate scoring as the fleet grows. Maintainability requires clear interfaces between simulator, policy, baseline, risk, explanation, and reporting modules. Data integrity requires a clear distinction between simulated and real observations.)
/Pg 25 0 R
