/P 217 0 R
/T (Three measures can limit the cost. First, candidate pruning keeps only the partners within a reasonable travel time of the order. Second, the action space can be defined per order, so the agent chooses a partner for one order at a time. Third, the cost matrix of the Hungarian Algorithm can be restricted to the pruned candidate set, which keeps the cubic complexity of the method manageable.)
/E (Three measures can limit the cost. First, candidate pruning keeps only the partners within a reasonable travel time of the order. Second, the action space can be defined per order, so the agent chooses a partner for one order at a time. Third, the cost matrix of the Hungarian Algorithm can be restricted to the pruned candidate set, which keeps the cubic complexity of the method manageable.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
570 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 217 0 R
/T (The effect of pruning on solution quality is an empirical question. A very tight pruning radius may remove the partner that would have been the best choice under heavy congestion, whereas a loose radius increases computation. The pruning parameter is therefore included in the configuration and examined in the sensitivity analysis.)
/E (The effect of pruning on solution quality is an empirical question. A very tight pruning radius may remove the partner that would have been the best choice under heavy congestion, whereas a loose radius increases computation. The pruning parameter is therefore included in the configuration and examined in the sensitivity analysis.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
