577 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 218 0 R
/E (constraints are defined. Next, a simulator generates orders, partner states, and traffic changes. State and reward functions are tested independently with controlled examples. A simple baseline is used to validate environment behaviour before training the DRL policy. The learned policy is evaluated on held-out scenarios and compared with baselines using common metrics.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 218 0 R
/E (Training and evaluation must remain separate. During training, the agent interacts with the environment and updates its policy from reward feedback. During evaluation, model parameters are frozen and scenarios are not used for further tuning. Multiple random seeds should be used, with means and variability reported. DQN and PPO are candidate approaches; the final choice should consider action-space compatibility, stability, training cost, and performance across scenarios.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
579 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
