580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 218 0 R
/E (At time t, state sI summarises pending order locations, deadlines and priorities; partner positions, availability and workload; and traffic, distance, and travel-time estimates. Numerical features should be scaled when their magnitudes differ substantially. The action aI assigns an order to an available partner. Only feasible pairs should be selectable. If no partner is eligible, the simulator should record a defined no-assignment or deferral event.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
581 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 218 0 R
/E (After an action, the simulator updates partner workload, task progress, order status, and time. It introduces new orders according to the scenario generator and changes traffic multipliers according to the selected traffic profile. Completed or overdue tasks update their records and contribute to the next reward. These transitions make assignment sequential because each decision changes the state for later orders.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
