/E (Weights should be tuned on training or validation scenarios and fixed before final evaluation. Sensitivity analysis should vary weights and record changes in delivery time, distance, workload, and risk. A single weighted reward can conceal trade-offs, so individual metrics must be reported alongside cumulative reward.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
589 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 219 0 R
/T (4.3.3 Reward Design Risks)
/E (4.3.3 Reward Design Risks)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
590 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 219 0 R
/E (An incomplete reward can encourage unintended behaviour. A distance penalty that is too large may favour short trips despite urgent deadlines; a workload penalty that is too strong may send an order to a distant partner. Tests should include high-priority orders, heavy congestion, few available partners, and simultaneous arrivals. Risk reduction must be measured as an outcome rather than inferred from the existence of a risk term.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
591 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 219 0 R
/T (4.4 DRL Agent and Baselines)
/E (4.4 DRL Agent and Baselines)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
592 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 219 0 R
/E (A neural network scores feasible assignment actions from the current state. DQN estimates action values, whereas PPO learns a policy through policy-gradient updates. The Hungarian Algorithm is applied to a cost matrix built from travel time and risk for a static snapshot. A nearest-partner rule selects the eligible partner with the smallest configured distance or travel-time estimate. All methods must use equivalent feasibility constraints and scenario information.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
593 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 219 0 R
/E (The Hungarian baseline is a reference for the matrix it receives, not proof that every DRL decision should match it. Agreement with the Hungarian assignment is a comparison metric, not absolute optimality in a dynamic environment. The nearest-partner rule establishes whether added model complexity provides practical value.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
