/S /H2
/P 220 0 R
/T (Each simulator step should update state consistently. A partner must not remain available after being assigned if the simulated rules say the partner is occupied. Paired comparisons should use the same traffic realisation for all methods. Evaluation logs should be retained so unexpected results can be investigated instead of being hidden by aggregate averages.)
/E (Each simulator step should update state consistently. A partner must not remain available after being assigned if the simulated rules say the partner is occupied. Paired comparisons should use the same traffic realisation for all methods. Evaluation logs should be retained so unexpected results can be investigated instead of being hidden by aggregate averages.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [10]
