612 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 220 0 R
/T (The scenario generator produces reproducible sequences of orders, partner states, and traffic conditions. A scenario is defined by the length of the simulated period, the number of partners, the mean order arrival rate, the spatial distribution of pickup and drop-off points, the distribution of deadline slack, the proportion of priority orders, and the traffic profile. All random draws use a seeded generator so that the same scenario can be repeated for every method.)
/E (The scenario generator produces reproducible sequences of orders, partner states, and traffic conditions. A scenario is defined by the length of the simulated period, the number of partners, the mean order arrival rate, the spatial distribution of pickup and drop-off points, the distribution of deadline slack, the proportion of priority orders, and the traffic profile. All random draws use a seeded generator so that the same scenario can be repeated for every method.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [12]
>>
