/E (Useful diagnostics include the episode return, the individual reward components, the proportion of on-time deliveries, the number of deferrals, the entropy of the policy for PPO, and the temporal-difference error for DQN. A policy that reaches a high return by neglecting one component, for example by ignoring workload balance, should be detected through these indicators and not accepted solely on the basis of the cumulative reward.)
