668 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 224 0 R
/E (A trained policy would select the action with the highest learned value, which also reflects expected future orders. If the explanation layer finds that the selected partner has a lower travel time than C and a lower risk than A, it produces a sentence of this kind and records the three compared values. The example is illustrative only; it does not represent a measured result, and the numbers in a real run depend on the scenario, the weights, and the trained policy.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [1]
>>
