/P 225 0 R
/E (Evaluation is planned across the same simulated scenarios for all methods. The metrics represent service quality, travel efficiency, utilisation, risk, and transparency. No measured values are reported because the source paper identifies the project as being at the design stage. Criterion Measure Purpose Delivery time Mean elapsed time per completed order Service speed On-time rate Orders completed by deadline / completed orders Deadline reliability Assignment agreement Agreement with Hungarian assignments on static snapshots Similarity to classical baseline Total distance Sum of partner travel distance Travel efficiency Workload distribution Spread or variance of work across partners Utilisation balance Risk score Mean normalised risk score of selected assignments Modelled operational risk Explanation coverage Assignments with explanation / total assignments Transparency Feasibility rate Valid assignments / attempted assignments Constraint handling)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
687 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 225 0 R
/T (5.2 Experimental Design)
/E (5.2 Experimental Design)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
688 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
/E (Experiments should cover light, moderate, and heavy order loads, as well as normal and congested traffic. Additional scenarios can vary partner availability, order location spread, deadline tightness, and the proportion of high-priority orders. The same scenario definitions and, where possible, random seeds should be used for every method. The DRL policy should be frozen during final evaluation, and the test set should not be used for tuning.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
689 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
