704 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (For each metric the report should present the mean over seeds together with a measure of spread, such as the standard deviation or a confidence interval. Because all methods are run on the same scenarios, paired comparisons are appropriate: the difference between two methods is computed for each seed and summarised, which reduces the effect of scenario difficulty.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
705 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (Where the number of seeds is small, non-parametric procedures or bootstrap intervals are preferable to assumptions of normality. A difference should be described as meaningful only if it is larger than the variability between seeds. Failed, infeasible, or truncated runs must be counted and reported rather than silently removed.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
