/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
729 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 228 0 R
/T (5.11 Reporting Format for Results)
/E (5.11 Reporting Format for Results)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
730 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (To keep the final results readable and comparable, a fixed reporting format is proposed. For each scenario group the report should contain a summary table with one row per method and one column per metric, giving the mean and the measure of spread over seeds. A second table should show paired differences between the learned policy and each baseline. Figures may show the distribution of delivery times, the distribution of orders across partners, and the evolution of the reward components during training.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
731 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (The text accompanying each table should describe what the numbers show without overstating them. Where the learned policy is better on one metric and worse on another, both facts must appear in the same paragraph. Where a result is within the variability between seeds, it should be described as inconclusive and not as an improvement.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
732 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 228 0 R
/T (5.12 Resources and Runtime Considerations)
/E (5.12 Resources and Runtime Considerations)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
733 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (The prototype is designed to run on a standard development computer. Training time depends on the network size, the number of environment steps, and the cost of each simulator step. Because the simulator is implemented in software and does not call external services, each step is inexpensive, and many episodes can be run in parallel for different seeds. The evaluation phase is also lightweight, since the policy is frozen and only needs to be applied.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
734 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (Runtime of the decision methods should be measured as well as quality. The time required to select an assignment is important in operations, where a recommendation must be returned quickly. The Hungarian Algorithm, the nearest-partner rule, and the neural network policy are expected to differ in decision latency, and this difference should be recorded under comparable hardware conditions.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
