/Title (SmartRoute AI is proposed as an explainable and risk-aware DRL framework for dynamic last-mile delivery assignment. It combines order requests, partner status, traffic estimates, distance, deadlines, and priority in a state representation. A DRL agent selects feasible assignments and receives reward feedback based on delay, distance, operational risk, and workload imbalance, with a bonus for on-time delivery. The Hungarian Algorithm provides a classical baseline and a nearest-partner rule offers a simple comparison point.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1600 0 R
/Next 1609 0 R
>>
endobj
1609 0 obj
<<
/Title (The framework includes an explanation layer that reports why a partner was selected using travel-time estimates, risk, and workload. Its modular architecture is intended for evaluation in a software simulator using repeatable scenarios and common metrics. Its contribution is the integration of dynamic learning, explicit risk awareness, workload balance, baseline comparison, and per-decision explanation in one proposed system. No numerical improvement is claimed because the supplied source material does not include completed simulation results.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1600 0 R
/Prev 1608 0 R
>>
