1719 0 obj
<<
/Title (Three measures can limit the cost. First, candidate pruning keeps only the partners within a reasonable travel time of the order. Second, the action space can be defined per order, so the agent chooses a partner for one order at a time. Third, the cost matrix of the Hungarian Algorithm can be restricted to the pruned candidate set, which keeps the cubic complexity of the method manageable.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1718 0 R
/Next 1715 0 R
>>
endobj
